<title>DUBAI: Aramco raises A-960 bunker fuel price, cuts A-888.</title>
<headline>Aramco raises A-960 bunker fuel price, cuts A-888.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has increased A-960 bunker fuel oil by 50 cents to $2 a tonne with effect June 5, the state company said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-960 bunkers from Ras Tanura and Damman is lifted to $104 a tonne and to $100.50 a tonne from Jeddah and Yanbu.</p>
<p>Aramco cut A-888 from the Gulf ports by $1 a tonne to $209 and by $7.50 to $189 a tonne from Red Sea ports.</p>
</text>
